{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QfUi8J9oVF2Us6mV3gNSmy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '核心\"DIF是RL-robust contamination signal\"假设不成立。5000+异构模型的response\n2\t  matrix严重违反IRT unidimensionality假设，architecture差异（encoder-only vs decoder-only vs\n3\t  MoE）制造了大量 spurious DIF，FPR膨胀至实用边界之外。真实contamination以partial memorization为主， ICC\n4\t  shift不足以在高噪声背景下被检出。RL-robustness优势不显著——传统方法在RL下虽然退化， 但DIF也退化，差距不足以支撑\"orthogonal\n5\t  signal\"叙事。需要pivot到negative-result framing 或剥离Claim 3做独立贡献。\n6\t\n7\t  '\n8\timagined_experiments:\n9\t- name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n10\t  plan_id: plan_001\n11\t  description: '对METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,055 models × 12,508 items)执行temporal\n12\t    cohort DIF分析， 以MMLU-CF为partial ground truth验证。\n13\t\n14\t    '\n15\t  expected_results:\n16\t    dif_tpr_delta_ge_1.4: 0.38\n17\t    dif_tpr_delta_ge_1.0: 0.18\n18\t    dif_fpr: 0.12\n19\t    mmlu_cf_correlation_with_dif_flags_phi: 0.09\n20\t    mmlu_cf_correlation_with_dif_flags_spearman: 0.07\n21\t    irt_model_fit_rmsea: 0.11\n22\t    irt_model_fit_cfi: 0.78\n23\t    n_items_flagged_ets_c: 1840\n24\t    n_items_flagged_ets_c_after_fpr_correction: 620\n25\t    cohort_size_pre2024: 1850\n26\t    cohort_size_post2024: 3205\n27\t    unidimensionality_test_p: 0.001\n28\t    item_discrimination_variance: 2.8\n29\t  result_rationale: '5055个模型跨越encoder-only (BERT-family)、decoder-only (GPT/LLaMA family)、MoE等根本不同\n30\t    的architecture，对MMLU items的response pattern受architecture驱动而非ability驱动。例如 decoder-only模型在long-context\n31\t    reasoning items上系统性优于encoder-only模型，这与contamination 无关但产生大量DIF。RMSEA=0.11远超可接受阈值(0.06)，CFI=0.78低于0.90标准，表明unidimensional\n32\t    IRT model严重misfit。在此背景下ETS C的effect-size threshold无法区分architecture-driven DIF\n33\t    和contamination-driven DIF，导致FPR膨胀至0.12。1840个items被flagged（15%的item pool）， 其中大部分是false\n34\t    positives。与MMLU-CF的correlation仅phi=0.09，接近random——因为MMLU-CF 本身的contamination annotation也有噪声（它只标注了\"显著修改\"的items，但并未验证原始items\n35\t    确实被contaminated），加上DIF flags被spurious signal淹没，两个noisy signal之间几乎无相关。\n36\t\n37\t    '\n38\t  tables:\n39\t  - title: 'Table 1: DIF Detection Performance on METABENCH MMLU (Worst Tier)'\n40\t    columns:\n41\t    - metric\n42\t    - pre2024_vs_post2024\n43\t    - annual_cohorts\n44\t    - sliding_window_6mo\n45\t    rows:\n46\t    - - TPR_delta_ge_1.4\n47\t      - 0.38\n48\t      - 0.31\n49\t      - 0.28\n50\t    - - TPR_delta_ge_1.0\n51\t      - 0.18\n52\t      - 0.14\n53\t      - 0.12\n54\t    - - FPR\n55\t      - 0.12\n56\t      - 0.14\n57\t      - 0.15\n58\t    - - F1_delta_ge_1.4\n59\t      - 0.33\n60\t      - 0.28\n61\t      - 0.25\n62\t    - - N_flagged_items\n63\t      - 1840\n64\t      - 2100\n65\t      - 2350\n66\t    - - MMLU-CF_phi_correlation\n67\t      - 0.09\n68\t      - 0.07\n69\t      - 0.06\n70\t  - title: 'Table 2: IRT Model Fit Diagnostics'\n71\t    columns:\n72\t    - fit_index\n73\t    - value\n74\t    - acceptable_threshold\n75\t    - verdict\n76\t    rows:\n77\t    - - RMSEA\n78\t      - 0.11\n79\t      - ≤0.06\n80\t      - FAIL\n81\t    - - CFI\n82\t      - 0.78\n83\t      - ≥0.90\n84\t      - FAIL\n85\t    - - TLI\n86\t      - 0.74\n87\t      - ≥0.90\n88\t      - FAIL\n89\t    - - SRMR\n90\t      - 0.09\n91\t      - ≤0.08\n92\t      - FAIL\n93\t    - - M2_p_value\n94\t      - <0.001\n95\t      - '>0.05'\n96\t      - FAIL\n97\t  figures_description:\n98\t  - 'Fig 1: ICC overlay of 20 highest-DIF items — curves show chaotic crossing patterns\n99\t    rather than clean uniform/non-uniform DIF, suggesting architecture heterogeneity\n100\t    rather than contamination as primary driver'\n101\t  - 'Fig 2: DIF effect size distribution — bimodal with large peak near zero and long\n102\t    right tail, but right tail items do not correlate with MMLU-CF contamination markers'\n103\t  - 'Fig 3: Heatmap of DIF flags × model architecture family — shows systematic DIF\n104\t    patterns aligned with architecture rather than temporal cohort'\n105\t  analysis: '核心发现：real data上IRT model严重misfit，DIF检测被architecture heterogeneity主导。\n106\t    Simulation中（Phase 2, N=100, δ=1.4, TPR=0.76）的performance无法迁移到real data， 因为simulation假设了unidimensional\n107\t    ability和homogeneous population——这在5055个异构模型上 完全不成立。FPR=0.12意味着每1000个clean items中有120个被错误flagged，在MMLU的12508个items\n108\t    上产生约1500个false positives，淹没了真正的contamination signal。MMLU-CF validation几乎 为negative（phi=0.09），无法作为DIF有效性的支撑证据。结论：categorical\n109\t    temporal cohort DIF 在heterogeneous model population上不可直接使用。\n110\t\n111\t    '\n112\t- name: rl_robustness_validation\n113\t  plan_id: plan_002\n114\t  description: '对比DIF与传统检测器在包含/不包含RL-trained模型的cohort上的表现差异。\n115\t\n116\t    '\n117\t  expected_results:\n118\t    dif_tpr_sft_only_delta_ge_1.4: 0.42\n119\t    dif_tpr_with_rl_delta_ge_1.4: 0.29\n120\t    dif_power_retention_ratio: 0.69\n121\t    traditional_mink_auroc_sft: 0.74\n122\t    traditional_mink_auroc_rl: 0.58\n123\t    traditional_constat_auroc_sft: 0.71\n124\t    traditional_constat_auroc_rl: 0.61\n125\t    traditional_dvd_auroc_sft: 0.68\n126\t    traditional_dvd_auroc_rl: 0.55\n127\t    dif_auroc_sft: 0.67\n128\t    dif_auroc_rl: 0.54\n129\t    dif_vs_traditional_auroc_gap_under_rl: 0.02\n130\t    n_rl_models_available: 12\n131\t    rl_model_cohort_size: 12\n132\t  result_rationale: 'RL-robustness假设的理论基础是\"DIF操作在group-level ICC上，RL只平移不改变ICC形状\"。但worst\n133\t    情景下RL不仅平移ICC——GRPO/PPO通过reward shaping改变了模型在不同difficulty levels上的response pattern，导致ICC形状本身变化（slope变陡或变平）。这使得RL-trained模型与SFT模型之间的ICC差异\n134\t    既来自contamination也来自training method，DIF无法区分二者。DIF在RL cohort下power从0.42降到 0.29（retention\n135\t    ratio=0.69），传统方法从~0.71降到~0.58。关键是DIF的降幅比例与传统方法相当， AUROC差距仅0.02——不足以支撑\"DIF是RL-orthogonal\n136\t    signal\"的核心论点。此外，可获取的RL模型 仅12个（METABENCH中标注为RL-trained的开源模型有限），cohort太小导致DIF统计功效本身就低，\n137\t    难以将power loss归因于RL vs simply small N。\n138\t\n139\t    '\n140\t  tables:\n141\t  - title: 'Table 3: RL-Robustness Comparison — DIF vs Traditional Detectors'\n142\t    columns:\n143\t    - method\n144\t    - auroc_sft_cohort\n145\t    - auroc_rl_cohort\n146\t    - retention_ratio\n147\t    - delta_auroc\n148\t    rows:\n149\t    - - DIF_ETS_C\n150\t      - 0.67\n151\t      - 0.54\n152\t      - 0.81\n153\t      - -0.13\n154\t    - - Min-K%\n155\t      - 0.74\n156\t      - 0.58\n157\t      - 0.78\n158\t      - -0.16\n159\t    - - ConStat\n160\t      - 0.71\n161\t      - 0.61\n162\t      - 0.86\n163\t      - -0.1\n164\t    - - DVD\n165\t      - 0.68\n166\t      - 0.55\n167\t      - 0.81\n168\t      - -0.13\n169\t    - - Perplexity\n170\t      - 0.69\n171\t      - 0.56\n172\t      - 0.81\n173\t      - -0.13\n174\t  - title: 'Table 4: DIF TPR Under SFT vs RL Cohorts'\n175\t    columns:\n176\t    - effect_size\n177\t    - tpr_sft_only\n178\t    - tpr_with_rl\n179\t    - retention\n180\t    rows:\n181\t    - - δ≥1.6\n182\t      - 0.48\n183\t      - 0.35\n184\t      - 0.73\n185\t    - - δ≥1.4\n186\t      - 0.42\n187\t      - 0.29\n188\t      - 0.69\n189\t    - - δ≥1.0\n190\t      - 0.2\n191\t      - 0.13\n192\t      - 0.65\n193\t    - - δ≥0.6\n194\t      - 0.09\n195\t      - 0.06\n196\t      - 0.67\n197\t  figures_description:\n198\t  - 'Fig 4: ROC curves for all 5 methods under SFT-only vs RL-included cohorts — all\n199\t    curves shift left/down under RL, with DIF and traditional methods degrading similarly\n200\t    (overlapping confidence intervals)'\n201\t  - 'Fig 5: ICC comparison for 5 known-contaminated items — RL models show altered\n202\t    slope (not just intercept shift), violating the theoretical basis of DIF robustness'\n203\t  analysis: 'DIF的RL-robustness优势不显著。AUROC under RL: DIF 0.54 vs best traditional 0.61\n204\t    (ConStat)， DIF实际上略差于ConStat。Power retention ratio 0.69落在worst tier预测范围[0.5, 0.75]内。\n205\t    核心问题：RL改变ICC形状（discrimination parameter a也变化），不仅仅是difficulty shift， 这意味着DIF的理论robustness\n206\t    argument不成立。加上RL cohort sample size仅12，统计结论的 可靠性本身存疑。无法支撑paper的headline claim。\n207\t\n208\t    '\n209\t- name: constat_perturbation_eval\n210\t  plan_id: plan_003a\n211\t  description: '独立评估ConStat-style perturbation testing在MMLU上的contamination检测能力。\n212\t\n213\t    '\n214\t  expected_results:\n215\t    constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_0.6: 0.32\n216\t    constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_1.0: 0.45\n217\t    constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_1.4: 0.55\n218\t    constat_tpr_rl_delta_ge_0.6: 0.11\n219\t    constat_tpr_rl_delta_ge_1.0: 0.18\n220\t    constat_fpr: 0.06\n221\t    constat_fdr_controlled_power: 0.28\n222\t    n_perturbation_items_generated: 220\n223\t    perturbation_quality_human_equiv_rate: 0.82\n224\t    paraphrase_semantic_similarity: 0.91\n225\t  result_rationale: 'ConStat在non-RL模型上有中等检测力（TPR=0.32 for δ≥0.6），因为SFT模型对verbatim\n226\t    memorized items的perturbation确实敏感——答对原题但答错改写题是contamination的合理信号。 但在worst tier下：(1)\n227\t    真实contamination多为partial memorization，模型可能只记住了answer pattern而非exact wording，对perturbation同样答对，降低sensitivity；(2)\n228\t    LLM paraphrase 生成的reformulations质量参差——82%被判为semantically equivalent，但18%引入了微妙的\n229\t    difficulty变化，增加noise；(3) RL模型对perturbation的sensitivity本身就低（RL鼓励 generalization），RL场景下TPR骤降至0.11。FDR-controlled\n230\t    power仅0.28，意味着在控制 false discovery rate后，能检出的contaminated items不到三分之一。作为standalone\n231\t    result 有一定baseline价值，但不足以独立成章。\n232\t\n233\t    '\n234\t  tables:\n235\t  - title: 'Table 5: ConStat Perturbation Detection by Effect Size and Model Type'\n236\t    columns:\n237\t    - effect_size\n238\t    - tpr_sft\n239\t    - tpr_rl\n240\t    - tpr_mixed\n241\t    - fpr\n242\t    rows:\n243\t    - - δ≥1.4\n244\t      - 0.55\n245\t      - 0.18\n246\t      - 0.38\n247\t      - 0.06\n248\t    - - δ≥1.0\n249\t      - 0.45\n250\t      - 0.14\n251\t      - 0.3\n252\t      - 0.06\n253\t    - - δ≥0.6\n254\t      - 0.32\n255\t      - 0.11\n256\t      - 0.22\n257\t      - 0.07\n258\t    - - δ≥0.4\n259\t      - 0.19\n260\t      - 0.08\n261\t      - 0.14\n262\t      - 0.07\n263\t  figures_description:\n264\t  - 'Fig 6: ConStat detection power as function of perturbation intensity — diminishing\n265\t    returns beyond moderate paraphrasing, suggesting contamination is not purely surface-form\n266\t    dependent'\n267\t  analysis: 'ConStat在non-RL场景下对large effects有moderate power，但RL场景下急剧退化。作为ensemble\n268\t    component对non-RL覆盖有限值，但无法作为RL-robust complement to DIF（两者在RL下都弱）。 FDR-controlled\n269\t    power 0.28意味着实际可用的detection capacity很有限。\n270\t\n271\t    '\n272\t- name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n273\t  plan_id: plan_003b\n274\t  description: '独立评估DVD generation variance方法在MMLU上检测variant contamination的能力。\n275\t\n276\t    '\n277\t  expected_results:\n278\t    dvd_tpr_variant_contamination: 0.22\n279\t    dvd_tpr_verbatim_contamination: 0.48\n280\t    dvd_tpr_partial_contamination: 0.12\n281\t    dvd_fpr: 0.09\n282\t    dvd_auroc_overall: 0.61\n283\t    n_models_evaluated: 13\n284\t    n_items_sampled: 500\n285\t    responses_per_item: 50\n286\t    bimodal_distribution_rate_contaminated: 0.18\n287\t    bimodal_distribution_rate_clean: 0.07\n288\t    gpu_hours_used: 65\n289\t  result_rationale: 'DVD的理论基础是contaminated items上model generation variance呈bimodal分布（有时recall\n290\t    memorized answer，有时不能）。在worst tier下：(1) variant contamination（题目被改写后 contaminated）信号最弱——模型对variant的memorization不稳定，generation\n291\t    variance与clean items差异小，TPR仅0.22；(2) partial contamination（仅记住部分信息）几乎无法检测（TPR=0.12），\n292\t    因为partial memory不产生bimodal response pattern，而是持续的uncertainty；(3) 即使verbatim contamination，TPR也仅0.48，因为很多模型在temperature\n293\t    sampling下对已知答案也表现stable （always correct），generation variance反而很低——与clean but easy\n294\t    items难以区分；(4) bimodal rate在contaminated items上仅18% vs clean items 7%，差异有统计显著性但effect\n295\t    size 太小无法做reliable detection。FPR=0.09偏高。总计消耗65 GPU hours，性价比低。\n296\t\n297\t    '\n298\t  tables:\n299\t  - title: 'Table 6: DVD Detection by Contamination Type'\n300\t    columns:\n301\t    - contamination_type\n302\t    - tpr\n303\t    - fpr\n304\t    - auroc\n305\t    - n_items\n306\t    rows:\n307\t    - - verbatim\n308\t      - 0.48\n309\t      - 0.09\n310\t      - 0.72\n311\t      - 120\n312\t    - - variant\n313\t      - 0.22\n314\t      - 0.09\n315\t      - 0.58\n316\t      - 180\n317\t    - - partial\n318\t      - 0.12\n319\t      - 0.09\n320\t      - 0.52\n321\t      - 200\n322\t    - - overall\n323\t      - 0.25\n324\t      - 0.09\n325\t      - 0.61\n326\t      - 500\n327\t  figures_description:\n328\t  - 'Fig 7: Generation variance distributions for contaminated vs clean items — overlapping\n329\t    distributions with small separation, bimodal pattern only visible in subset of\n330\t    verbatim contamination cases'\n331\t  analysis: 'DVD对variant contamination的检测力远低于预期（TPR=0.22 vs 论文claim需要的高coverage）。\n332\t    核心问题是real-world contamination不产生clean bimodal response pattern——partial memorization\n333\t    导致diffuse variance而非bimodal variance。GPU开销大但回报低，作为ensemble component 贡献有限。\n334\t\n335\t    '\n336\t- name: ensemble_fusion\n337\t  plan_id: plan_003c\n338\t  description: '将DIF + ConStat + DVD融合为多信号ensemble，评估覆盖度和precision。\n339\t\n340\t    '\n341\t  expected_results:\n342\t    ensemble_tpr_full_spectrum: 0.42\n343\t    ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_1.4: 0.52\n344\t    ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_1.0: 0.3\n345\t    ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_0.6: 0.18\n346\t    ensemble_fpr: 0.11\n347\t    ensemble_f1: 0.35\n348\t    majority_voting_tpr: 0.38\n349\t    weighted_fusion_tpr: 0.42\n350\t    signal_correlation_dif_constat: 0.61\n351\t    signal_correlation_dif_dvd: 0.54\n352\t    signal_correlation_constat_dvd: 0.58\n353\t    unique_items_flagged_by_only_one_signal_pct: 0.15\n354\t    items_flagged_by_all_three_pct: 0.42\n355\t  result_rationale: 'Ensemble假设三个signal互补——DIF覆盖large effects+RL场景，ConStat覆盖non-RL\n356\t    medium effects， DVD覆盖variant contamination。但worst tier下：(1) 三个signal之间correlation高（r=0.54-0.61），\n357\t    表明它们largely flag同一批items而非互补覆盖不同盲区；(2) 仅15%的items被unique地由某一个 signal单独检出，说明\"互补覆盖\"理论不成立——各signal的failure\n358\t    modes相关（都在partial/medium effect上失败）；(3) 42%的items被三个signal同时flag，说明easy cases三者都能检出但hard\n359\t    cases 三者都漏检；(4) FPR=0.11，majority voting无法有效压低FPR因为false positives也呈相关模式 （architecture-driven\n360\t    spurious DIF也往往在perturbation testing中产生false positive）。 Weighted fusion比majority\n361\t    voting略好（TPR 0.42 vs 0.38）但提升有限。整体full-spectrum TPR=0.42落在worst tier [0.35, 0.6]范围内，不足以作为实用detection\n362\t    system。\n363\t\n364\t    '\n365\t  tables:\n366\t  - title: 'Table 7: Ensemble vs Individual Signal Performance'\n367\t    columns:\n368\t    - method\n369\t    - tpr_ge_1.4\n370\t    - tpr_ge_1.0\n371\t    - tpr_ge_0.6\n372\t    - fpr\n373\t    - f1\n374\t    rows:\n375\t    - - DIF_only\n376\t      - 0.38\n377\t      - 0.18\n378\t      - 0.09\n379\t      - 0.12\n380\t      - 0.25\n381\t    - - ConStat_only\n382\t      - 0.38\n383\t      - 0.3\n384\t      - 0.22\n385\t      - 0.06\n386\t      - 0.32\n387\t    - - DVD_only\n388\t      - 0.25\n389\t      - 0.15\n390\t      - 0.1\n391\t      - 0.09\n392\t      - 0.18\n393\t    - - Majority_2of3\n394\t      - 0.38\n395\t      - 0.19\n396\t      - 0.11\n397\t      - 0.05\n398\t      - 0.3\n399\t    - - Weighted_fusion\n400\t      - 0.52\n401\t      - 0.3\n402\t      - 0.18\n403\t      - 0.11\n404\t      - 0.35\n405\t  - title: 'Table 8: Signal Correlation Matrix'\n406\t    columns:\n407\t    - signal_pair\n408\t    - pearson_r\n409\t    - overlap_in_flagged_items_pct\n410\t    rows:\n411\t    - - DIF-ConStat\n412\t      - 0.61\n413\t      - 0.68\n414\t    - - DIF-DVD\n415\t      - 0.54\n416\t      - 0.59\n417\t    - - ConStat-DVD\n418\t      - 0.58\n419\t      - 0.63\n420\t  figures_description:\n421\t  - 'Fig 8: Venn diagram of items flagged by each signal — large central overlap,\n422\t    small unique regions, contradicting the ''complementary coverage'' hypothesis'\n423\t  - 'Fig 9: Ensemble TPR as function of effect size — flat improvement over best individual\n424\t    signal, no ''coverage completion'' effect at medium/low effects'\n425\t  analysis: 'Ensemble的\"互补覆盖\"核心假设不成立。信号间高相关（0.54-0.61）意味着ensemble主要在置信度上 提升（对已检出items更confident）而非在覆盖度上提升（检出新items）。Weighted\n426\t    fusion的TPR=0.42 仅比best individual signal (ConStat 0.30 at δ≥1.0) 提升有限，且FPR=0.11偏高。这个ensemble\n427\t    不能作为\"full-spectrum detection system\"呈现——更准确的描述是\"three weak signals with correlated\n428\t    failure modes\"。\n429\t\n430\t    '\n431\t- name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n432\t  plan_id: plan_004\n433\t  description: '在GSM8K上复制DIF分析，以GSM1K作为contamination ground truth进行交叉验证。\n434\t\n435\t    '\n436\t  expected_results:\n437\t    gsm8k_gsm1k_gap_dif_correlation_spearman: 0.11\n438\t    gsm8k_gsm1k_gap_dif_correlation_pearson: 0.08\n439\t    dif_tpr_gsm8k_delta_ge_1.4: 0.3\n440\t    dif_fpr_gsm8k: 0.13\n441\t    n_models_with_both_gsm8k_gsm1k: 48\n442\t    irt_model_fit_rmsea_gsm8k: 0.09\n443\t    gsm8k_item_discrimination_mean: 0.85\n444\t    gsm1k_gap_mean_across_models: 0.07\n445\t    gsm1k_gap_std: 0.11\n446\t    n_items_gsm8k_analyzed: 1319\n447\t  result_rationale: 'GSM8K validation在worst tier下面临多重困难：(1) 可获取的同时有GSM8K和GSM1K结果的模型仅\n448\t    约48个（远少于MMLU的5055个），DIF统计功效严重不足；(2) GSM8K是math benchmark，item discrimination偏低(mean\n449\t    a=0.85)因为数学题的对错更binary、less informative about latent ability gradient，这直接降低DIF\n450\t    detection power；(3) GSM8K-GSM1K gap本身noisy（std=0.11 vs mean=0.07），gap的model-level\n451\t    variance高说明contamination不是uniform的——不同模型 contamination程度差异大，但DIF是item-level metric，model-level\n452\t    gap与item-level DIF flag之间的mapping本就不是直接对应的；(4) GSM1K作为ground truth的assumption是\"GSM1K\n453\t    uncontaminated\"，但GSM1K发布后也可能被contaminated，ground truth本身会退化。 Spearman rho=0.11几乎无相关，无法支撑cross-benchmark\n454\t    generalizability。\n455\t\n456\t    '\n457\t  tables:\n458\t  - title: 'Table 9: GSM8K Cross-Validation Results'\n459\t    columns:\n460\t    - metric\n461\t    - value\n462\t    - worst_tier_range\n463\t    - verdict\n464\t    rows:\n465\t    - - DIF_TPR_δ≥1.4\n466\t      - 0.3\n467\t      - 0.25-0.50\n468\t      - IN_RANGE\n469\t    - - DIF_FPR\n470\t      - 0.13\n471\t      - 0.08-0.15\n472\t      - IN_RANGE\n473\t    - - GSM8K-GSM1K_gap_correlation\n474\t      - 0.11\n475\t      - 0.0-0.18\n476\t      - IN_RANGE\n477\t    - - N_models\n478\t      - 48\n479\t      - ≥50 desired\n480\t      - INSUFFICIENT\n481\t    - - IRT_fit_RMSEA\n482\t      - 0.09\n483\t      - ≤0.06\n484\t      - FAIL\n485\t  figures_description:\n486\t  - 'Fig 10: Scatter plot of per-model GSM8K-GSM1K gap vs number of DIF-flagged items\n487\t    in that model''s performance — near-zero correlation with wide scatter'\n488\t  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark validation为negative result。GSM8K上DIF表现与MMLU类似（low TPR,\n489\t    high FPR）， 且与GSM1K ground truth的correlation接近零（rho=0.11）。样本量不足（48 models vs desired\n490\t    50+） 进一步削弱统计结论的可靠性。这不能作为DIF generalizability的支撑证据。\n491\t\n492\t    '\n493\t- name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n494\t  plan_id: plan_005\n495\t  description: '在METABENCH MMLU数据上拟合bifactor IRT模型，选取anchor items，执行equating pilot。\n496\t\n497\t    '\n498\t  expected_results:\n499\t    bifactor_convergence: partial\n500\t    bifactor_iterations_to_convergence: 8500\n501\t    bifactor_n_items_converged: 9200\n502\t    bifactor_n_items_failed: 3308\n503\t    general_factor_variance_explained: 0.35\n504\t    n_specific_factors: 57\n505\t    specific_factor_avg_loading: 0.28\n506\t    anchor_item_n_selected: 380\n507\t    anchor_item_stability_mean_dif: 0.15\n508\t    equating_spearman_rho_before: 0.82\n509\t    equating_spearman_rho_after: 0.85\n510\t    equating_rank_displacement_mean: 3.2\n511\t    equating_rank_displacement_p95: 12\n512\t    score_reliability_original: 0.94\n513\t    score_reliability_equated: 0.89\n514\t  result_rationale: 'Bifactor model在5055个异构模型上面临严重的estimation challenge：(1) 57个MMLU\n515\t    subjects作为 specific factors，加上1个general factor，parameter space巨大（~12500 items\n516\t    × 3 parameters × 58 factors），在worst tier下3308个items（26%）的参数估计不收敛或产生Heywood cases\n517\t    （negative variance estimates）；(2) general factor仅解释35%的variance——这意味着MMLU 不是primarily\n518\t    measuring一个general LLM ability，而是highly multidimensional的，bifactor structure不是good\n519\t    fit；(3) specific factor loadings平均仅0.28，说明subject-level factors 也很弱，很多items不清晰地load在任何factor上——factor\n520\t    structure不可解释；(4) 尽管如此， equating在技术上仍可执行：选出380个stable anchor items（无DIF、参数估计收敛），equating\n521\t    后ranking correlation从0.82提升到0.85，但这个提升幅度小（Δ=0.03），且基线rho=0.82 已低于Claim 3要求的0.95标准。Equating没有失败但也没有convincingly成功——它能small\n522\t    improvement ranking stability，但不能达到psychometric equivalence的标准。\n523\t\n524\t    '\n525\t  tables:\n526\t  - title: 'Table 10: Bifactor IRT Model Fit and Equating Results'\n527\t    columns:\n528\t    - metric\n529\t    - value\n530\t    - target\n531\t    - verdict\n532\t    rows:\n533\t    - - convergence_rate\n534\t      - 73.5%\n535\t      - ≥95%\n536\t      - FAIL\n537\t    - - general_factor_variance\n538\t      - 0.35\n539\t      - ≥0.50\n540\t      - WEAK\n541\t    - - anchor_items_available\n542\t      - 380\n543\t      - ≥500\n544\t      - MARGINAL\n545\t    - - equating_rho\n546\t      - 0.85\n547\t      - ≥0.95\n548\t      - FAIL\n549\t    - - rank_displacement_p95\n550\t      - 12\n551\t      - ≤5\n552\t      - FAIL\n553\t    - - score_reliability_post\n554\t      - 0.89\n555\t      - ≥0.92\n556\t      - MARGINAL\n557\t  - title: 'Table 11: Factor Structure Summary'\n558\t    columns:\n559\t    - factor_type\n560\t    - n_factors\n561\t    - mean_loading\n562\t    - pct_items_loading_gt_0.3\n563\t    rows:\n564\t    - - general\n565\t      - 1\n566\t      - 0.42\n567\t      - 62%\n568\t    - - specific_STEM\n569\t      - 14\n570\t      - 0.31\n571\t      - 38%\n572\t    - - specific_humanities\n573\t      - 18\n574\t      - 0.26\n575\t      - 29%\n576\t    - - specific_social_science\n577\t      - 15\n578\t      - 0.28\n579\t      - 33%\n580\t    - - specific_other\n581\t      - 10\n582\t      - 0.24\n583\t      - 25%\n584\t  figures_description:\n585\t  - 'Fig 11: Scree plot showing eigenvalues — no clear elbow, gradual decline suggesting\n586\t    no dominant general factor'\n587\t  - 'Fig 12: Equated vs original model rankings — scatter with regression line showing\n588\t    moderate but not strong agreement (rho=0.85), notable outliers at tails'\n589\t  analysis: 'Bifactor model在异构LLM population上partially converges但factor structure不清晰。\n590\t    General factor太弱（35% variance）挑战了\"MMLU measures a coherent construct\"的前提。 Equating产生了modest\n591\t    improvement (0.82→0.85) 但远未达到psychometric equivalence标准 (0.95)。作为独立贡献（Claim 3\n592\t    standalone），这个result需要被framed为\"benchmark multidimensionality的empirical characterization\"而非\"successful\n593\t    equating\"。可能可以 pivot到Growing Pains style的\"LLM evaluation需要multidimensional IRT\"叙事。\n594\t\n595\t    '\n596\t- name: item_generation_calibration\n597\t  plan_id: plan_006\n598\t  description: '生成替代items并通过student simulation进行calibration，评估difficulty estimation质量。\n599\t\n600\t    '\n601\t  expected_results:\n602\t    n_items_generated: 150\n603\t    n_items_passing_quality_filter: 112\n604\t    difficulty_calibration_rho_student_sim: 0.48\n605\t    difficulty_calibration_rho_prompt_based: 0.22\n606\t    difficulty_mae_student_sim: 0.85\n607\t    difficulty_mae_prompt_based: 1.45\n608\t    discrimination_calibration_rho: 0.31\n609\t    construct_alignment_rate: 0.72\n610\t    holdout_validation_rho: 0.44\n611\t    student_sim_correlation_with_real_models: 0.52\n612\t    gpu_hours_used: 180\n613\t  result_rationale: 'Item generation在worst tier下的核心问题：(1) Student simulation (arXiv\n614\t    2601.09953) 的difficulty estimation在MMLU上表现弱于其在其他benchmarks上的reported results——因为\n615\t    MMLU covers 57 diverse subjects，student simulation的\"simulated students\"是single\n616\t    LLM 做capability ablation，但不同subject需要不同type的knowledge/reasoning，single-model simulation无法capture\n617\t    this diversity，rho=0.48；(2) Prompt-based difficulty targeting 依然很差（rho=0.22），与文献报告一致；(3)\n618\t    Student simulation比prompt-based好（0.48 vs 0.22） 但absolute accuracy仍不够——difficulty\n619\t    MAE=0.85 logits意味着平均偏差接近1个标准差， 生成的items实际difficulty与target可能差1-2个difficulty band；(4)\n620\t    Discrimination calibration 更差（rho=0.31），因为discrimination是更subtle的item property，依赖于item如何在不同ability\n621\t    levels上区分模型，student simulation几乎无法capture；(5) Construct alignment rate 72% 意味着28%的generated\n622\t    items虽然表面上是同一subject但实际测量的cognitive process不同 （e.g., 要求recall的item被替换为要求reasoning的item）。这些result不支撑\"calibrated\n623\t    item regeneration\"的claim，但student sim vs prompt-based的comparison本身有文献价值。\n624\t\n625\t    '\n626\t  tables:\n627\t  - title: 'Table 12: Item Calibration Comparison'\n628\t    columns:\n629\t    - method\n630\t    - difficulty_rho\n631\t    - difficulty_mae\n632\t    - discrimination_rho\n633\t    - construct_alignment\n634\t    rows:\n635\t    - - student_simulation\n636\t      - 0.48\n637\t      - 0.85\n638\t      - 0.31\n639\t      - 72%\n640\t    - - prompt_based\n641\t      - 0.22\n642\t      - 1.45\n643\t      - 0.18\n644\t      - 65%\n645\t    - - random_baseline\n646\t      - 0.05\n647\t      - 1.8\n648\t      - 0.08\n649\t      - 45%\n650\t  - title: 'Table 13: Holdout Validation on 30 Models'\n651\t    columns:\n652\t    - metric\n653\t    - student_sim\n654\t    - prompt_based\n655\t    rows:\n656\t    - - difficulty_rank_correlation\n657\t      - 0.44\n658\t      - 0.19\n659\t    - - score_equivalence_rho\n660\t      - 0.78\n661\t      - 0.68\n662\t    - - ranking_preservation_top10\n663\t      - 70%\n664\t      - 50%\n665\t  figures_description:\n666\t  - 'Fig 13: Predicted vs actual item difficulty — student simulation shows moderate\n667\t    correlation but with substantial scatter, especially for very hard items'\n668\t  - 'Fig 14: Distribution of difficulty estimation errors — student simulation has\n669\t    tighter but still wide distribution (SD=0.85) compared to prompt-based (SD=1.2)'\n670\t  analysis: 'Student simulation在MMLU上的calibration quality不足以支撑reliable item replacement。\n671\t    Difficulty rho=0.48意味着替换后的benchmark与原版在difficulty ordering上只有moderate agreement，不够做psychometric\n672\t    equating。但student sim vs prompt-based的comparison （0.48 vs 0.22）以及failure mode\n673\t    analysis（which subjects/difficulty ranges失败） 仍有独立的文献贡献价值。\n674\t\n675\t    '\n676\t- name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n677\t  plan_id: plan_007\n678\t  description: '实现cumulative Bayesian DIF priors，模拟4次successive benchmark administrations的power积累。\n679\t\n680\t    '\n681\t  expected_results:\n682\t    single_admin_power_delta_1.0: 0.15\n683\t    cumulative_power_2_admins_delta_1.0: 0.22\n684\t    cumulative_power_3_admins_delta_1.0: 0.3\n685\t    cumulative_power_4_admins_delta_1.0: 0.38\n686\t    single_admin_power_delta_1.4: 0.35\n687\t    cumulative_power_4_admins_delta_1.4: 0.55\n688\t    bayesian_fpr_single: 0.1\n689\t    bayesian_fpr_cumulative_4: 0.08\n690\t    prior_informativeness_shrinkage: 0.45\n691\t  result_rationale: 'Bayesian cumulative priors在worst tier下受到两个因素制约：(1) 如果baseline\n692\t    single-admin power已经很低（0.15 for δ=1.0，因为real data上IRT model misfit），那么cumulative\n693\t    evidence accumulation的起点就低——Bayesian updating from a weak prior仍然是weak， 4次admin后仅到0.38（远低于theoretical\n694\t    prediction of 0.70）；(2) Prior informativeness 受model population heterogeneity影响——如果每次administration的model\n695\t    cohort composition 很不同（architecture mix变化），prior从上一admin的posterior transfer不顺畅，shrinkage\n696\t    factor高达0.45（理想应<0.2），意味着prior对posterior的influence被data overwhelm但data 本身noisy。FPR从0.10降至0.08是modest\n697\t    improvement。总体而言，cumulative approach能 提升power但幅度远不如simulated homogeneous scenarios中的预期。\n698\t\n699\t    '\n700\t  tables:\n701\t  - title: 'Table 14: Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power Accumulation'\n702\t    columns:\n703\t    - n_administrations\n704\t    - power_delta_1.0\n705\t    - power_delta_1.4\n706\t    - fpr\n707\t    rows:\n708\t    - - 1\n709\t      - 0.15\n710\t      - 0.35\n711\t      - 0.1\n712\t    - - 2\n713\t      - 0.22\n714\t      - 0.42\n715\t      - 0.09\n716\t    - - 3\n717\t      - 0.3\n718\t      - 0.49\n719\t      - 0.09\n720\t    - - 4\n721\t      - 0.38\n722\t      - 0.55\n723\t      - 0.08\n724\t  figures_description:\n725\t  - 'Fig 15: Power accumulation curves — shallow slope compared to theoretical prediction\n726\t    (dashed line), gap widens with each administration due to population heterogeneity'\n727\t  analysis: 'Cumulative Bayesian approach有边际收益但无法rescue低baseline power。4 admins后power\n728\t    仅从0.15升至0.38 (δ=1.0)，远低于theoretical 0.70。Population heterogeneity导致prior transfer效率低。作为P2\n729\t    experiment，结果不改变overall narrative但进一步确认了DIF在 heterogeneous LLM population上的fundamental\n730\t    limitations。\n731\t\n732\t    '\n733\t- name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n734\t  plan_id: plan_008\n735\t  description: '分析benchmark在progressive item replacement下的validity degradation。\n736\t\n737\t    '\n738\t  expected_results:\n739\t    ranking_stability_5pct_replaced: 0.94\n740\t    ranking_stability_10pct_replaced: 0.88\n741\t    ranking_stability_20pct_replaced: 0.79\n742\t    ranking_stability_50pct_replaced: 0.62\n743\t    score_reliability_5pct: 0.92\n744\t    score_reliability_10pct: 0.88\n745\t    score_reliability_20pct: 0.81\n746\t    score_reliability_50pct: 0.67\n747\t    construct_coverage_5pct: 0.97\n748\t    construct_coverage_10pct: 0.93\n749\t    construct_coverage_20pct: 0.85\n750\t    construct_coverage_50pct: 0.71\n751\t    critical_replacement_threshold: 0.12\n752\t  result_rationale: 'Graceful degradation在worst tier下退化快于预期因为：(1) Item calibration\n753\t    quality差 （difficulty rho=0.48 from plan_006），替换items的psychometric properties与被替换items\n754\t    不匹配，每次替换引入的error大于calibration error budget允许的范围；(2) Bifactor equating 不充分（rho=0.85\n755\t    from plan_005），equating本身引入systematic bias，累积到20%替换时 ranking stability降至0.79（如果equating完美，应维持在0.92+）；(3)\n756\t    Construct coverage degradation因为28%的generated items construct alignment有问题（from\n757\t    plan_006）， 20%替换时约5-6%的items测量不同construct，coverage降至0.85。Critical threshold（ranking\n758\t    rho降至0.90以下的替换比例）仅12%——意味着实际上只能安全替换约1500个items，远少于 potential contaminated items的数量（如果FPR=0.12则约1800个被flag）。\n759\t\n760\t    '\n761\t  tables:\n762\t  - title: 'Table 15: Validity Degradation Under Progressive Replacement'\n763\t    columns:\n764\t    - replacement_pct\n765\t    - ranking_rho\n766\t    - reliability\n767\t    - construct_coverage\n768\t    rows:\n769\t    - - 0% (baseline)\n770\t      - 1.0\n771\t      - 0.94\n772\t      - 1.0\n773\t    - - 5%\n774\t      - 0.94\n775\t      - 0.92\n776\t      - 0.97\n777\t    - - 10%\n778\t      - 0.88\n779\t      - 0.88\n780\t      - 0.93\n781\t    - - 20%\n782\t      - 0.79\n783\t      - 0.81\n784\t      - 0.85\n785\t    - - 50%\n786\t      - 0.62\n787\t      - 0.67\n788\t      - 0.71\n789\t  - title: 'Table 16: Critical Thresholds'\n790\t    columns:\n791\t    - validity_criterion\n792\t    - threshold_value\n793\t    - max_safe_replacement_pct\n794\t    rows:\n795\t    - - ranking_rho_≥0.90\n796\t      - 0.9\n797\t      - 12%\n798\t    - - reliability_≥0.90\n799\t      - 0.9\n800\t      - 7%\n801\t    - - construct_coverage_≥0.90\n802\t      - 0.9\n803\t      - 14%\n804\t    - - all_criteria_met\n805\t      - '-'\n806\t      - 7%\n807\t  figures_description:\n808\t  - 'Fig 16: Validity metrics as function of replacement rate — all three metrics\n809\t    degrade faster than linear, with reliability being the binding constraint (7%)'\n810\t  analysis: 'Graceful degradation analysis表明在当前calibration quality下，只能安全替换7%的items\n811\t    （约875个items，满足所有validity criteria）。这远不足以构成practical \"self-healing\" benchmark——如果检测到的contaminated\n812\t    items超过7%，replacement会损害benchmark validity。 这是对Claim 3的严重限制，但degradation curve本身是有价值的empirical\n813\t    contribution， 可以frame为\"item replacement的practical bounds\"。\n814\t\n815\t    '\n816\t- name: item_focused_trees\n817\t  plan_id: plan_009\n818\t  description: '实现Item-Focused Trees，将model release date作为continuous covariate替代categorical\n819\t    cohort DIF。\n820\t\n821\t    '\n822\t  expected_results:\n823\t    ift_tpr_delta_ge_1.4: 0.33\n824\t    ift_tpr_delta_ge_1.0: 0.16\n825\t    ift_fpr: 0.1\n826\t    ift_vs_categorical_dif_tpr_delta: -0.05\n827\t    ift_computation_time_hours: 18\n828\t    n_splits_found: 3.2\n829\t    split_dates_concentration: 2023-06 to 2024-01\n830\t    overfitting_cross_val_tpr_drop: 0.12\n831\t  result_rationale: 'Item-Focused Trees理论上避免arbitrary cohort splits，但在worst tier下：(1)\n832\t    Release date 作为continuous covariate与contamination的关系不是smooth monotonic的——contamination是\n833\t    event-driven（某次data leak），不是gradual trend，IFT的tree structure可以capture这个 但容易overfit到特定split\n834\t    points；(2) Cross-validation显示TPR drop=0.12，说明overfitting significant；(3) 在model\n835\t    heterogeneity高的情况下，IFT实际上比categorical DIF表现略差 （TPR差-0.05），因为tree splitting在high-noise环境下容易找到spurious\n836\t    splits——3.2个 average splits集中在2023年中到2024年初，这恰好是architecture transition period\n837\t    （GPT-4发布后大量models涌现），tree可能在capture architecture shift而非contamination。 FPR=0.10比categorical\n838\t    DIF（0.12）略低，但improvement不显著。Computation cost 18 hours 因为per-item tree fitting在12508\n839\t    items上。\n840\t\n841\t    '\n842\t  tables:\n843\t  - title: 'Table 17: Item-Focused Trees vs Categorical DIF'\n844\t    columns:\n845\t    - metric\n846\t    - categorical_dif\n847\t    - ift\n848\t    - delta\n849\t    rows:\n850\t    - - TPR_δ≥1.4\n851\t      - 0.38\n852\t      - 0.33\n853\t      - -0.05\n854\t    - - TPR_δ≥1.0\n855\t      - 0.18\n856\t      - 0.16\n857\t      - -0.02\n858\t    - - FPR\n859\t      - 0.12\n860\t      - 0.1\n861\t      - -0.02\n862\t    - - F1\n863\t      - 0.25\n864\t      - 0.24\n865\t      - -0.01\n866\t    - - computation_hours\n867\t      - 0.5\n868\t      - 18\n869\t      - '+17.5'\n870\t  figures_description:\n871\t  - 'Fig 17: IFT split point distribution — concentration around architecture transition\n872\t    periods rather than known contamination events'\n873\t  analysis: IFT未能改善DIF detection。Split points与architecture transitions而非contamination\n874\t    events 对齐，进一步证实model heterogeneity是dominant signal source。计算成本高36倍但无performance\n875\t    gain。作为P2 experiment，结论是negative：continuous covariate treatment不解决fundamental\n876\t    问题。\n877\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"570af1f9-c3cd-4db4-aa61-2d20e9ee2d29","uuid":"8f95c09c-4f71-4ccb-8662-3b9677b25de5","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:24:56.096Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T194223/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '核心\"DIF是RL-robust contamination signal\"假设不成立。5000+异构模型的response\n  matrix严重违反IRT unidimensionality假设，architecture差异（encoder-only vs decoder-only vs\n  MoE）制造了大量 spurious DIF，FPR膨胀至实用边界之外。真实contamination以partial memorization为主， ICC\n  shift不足以在高噪声背景下被检出。RL-robustness优势不显著——传统方法在RL下虽然退化， 但DIF也退化，差距不足以支撑\"orthogonal\n  signal\"叙事。需要pivot到negative-result framing 或剥离Claim 3做独立贡献。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: '对METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,055 models × 12,508 items)执行temporal\n    cohort DIF分析， 以MMLU-CF为partial ground truth验证。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dif_tpr_delta_ge_1.4: 0.38\n    dif_tpr_delta_ge_1.0: 0.18\n    dif_fpr: 0.12\n    mmlu_cf_correlation_with_dif_flags_phi: 0.09\n    mmlu_cf_correlation_with_dif_flags_spearman: 0.07\n    irt_model_fit_rmsea: 0.11\n    irt_model_fit_cfi: 0.78\n    n_items_flagged_ets_c: 1840\n    n_items_flagged_ets_c_after_fpr_correction: 620\n    cohort_size_pre2024: 1850\n    cohort_size_post2024: 3205\n    unidimensionality_test_p: 0.001\n    item_discrimination_variance: 2.8\n  result_rationale: '5055个模型跨越encoder-only (BERT-family)、decoder-only (GPT/LLaMA family)、MoE等根本不同\n    的architecture，对MMLU items的response pattern受architecture驱动而非ability驱动。例如 decoder-only模型在long-context\n    reasoning items上系统性优于encoder-only模型，这与contamination 无关但产生大量DIF。RMSEA=0.11远超可接受阈值(0.06)，CFI=0.78低于0.90标准，表明unidimensional\n    IRT model严重misfit。在此背景下ETS C的effect-size threshold无法区分architecture-driven DIF\n    和contamination-driven DIF，导致FPR膨胀至0.12。1840个items被flagged（15%的item pool）， 其中大部分是false\n    positives。与MMLU-CF的correlation仅phi=0.09，接近random——因为MMLU-CF 本身的contamination annotation也有噪声（它只标注了\"显著修改\"的items，但并未验证原始items\n    确实被contaminated），加上DIF flags被spurious signal淹没，两个noisy signal之间几乎无相关。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 1: DIF Detection Performance on METABENCH MMLU (Worst Tier)'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - pre2024_vs_post2024\n    - annual_cohorts\n    - sliding_window_6mo\n    rows:\n    - - TPR_delta_ge_1.4\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.28\n    - - TPR_delta_ge_1.0\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.12\n    - - FPR\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.15\n    - - F1_delta_ge_1.4\n      - 0.33\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.25\n    - - N_flagged_items\n      - 1840\n      - 2100\n      - 2350\n    - - MMLU-CF_phi_correlation\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.07\n      - 0.06\n  - title: 'Table 2: IRT Model Fit Diagnostics'\n    columns:\n    - fit_index\n    - value\n    - acceptable_threshold\n    - verdict\n    rows:\n    - - RMSEA\n      - 0.11\n      - ≤0.06\n      - FAIL\n    - - CFI\n      - 0.78\n      - ≥0.90\n      - FAIL\n    - - TLI\n      - 0.74\n      - ≥0.90\n      - FAIL\n    - - SRMR\n      - 0.09\n      - ≤0.08\n      - FAIL\n    - - M2_p_value\n      - <0.001\n      - '>0.05'\n      - FAIL\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 1: ICC overlay of 20 highest-DIF items — curves show chaotic crossing patterns\n    rather than clean uniform/non-uniform DIF, suggesting architecture heterogeneity\n    rather than contamination as primary driver'\n  - 'Fig 2: DIF effect size distribution — bimodal with large peak near zero and long\n    right tail, but right tail items do not correlate with MMLU-CF contamination markers'\n  - 'Fig 3: Heatmap of DIF flags × model architecture family — shows systematic DIF\n    patterns aligned with architecture rather than temporal cohort'\n  analysis: '核心发现：real data上IRT model严重misfit，DIF检测被architecture heterogeneity主导。\n    Simulation中（Phase 2, N=100, δ=1.4, TPR=0.76）的performance无法迁移到real data， 因为simulation假设了unidimensional\n    ability和homogeneous population——这在5055个异构模型上 完全不成立。FPR=0.12意味着每1000个clean items中有120个被错误flagged，在MMLU的12508个items\n    上产生约1500个false positives，淹没了真正的contamination signal。MMLU-CF validation几乎 为negative（phi=0.09），无法作为DIF有效性的支撑证据。结论：categorical\n    temporal cohort DIF 在heterogeneous model population上不可直接使用。\n\n    '\n- name: rl_robustness_validation\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '对比DIF与传统检测器在包含/不包含RL-trained模型的cohort上的表现差异。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dif_tpr_sft_only_delta_ge_1.4: 0.42\n    dif_tpr_with_rl_delta_ge_1.4: 0.29\n    dif_power_retention_ratio: 0.69\n    traditional_mink_auroc_sft: 0.74\n    traditional_mink_auroc_rl: 0.58\n    traditional_constat_auroc_sft: 0.71\n    traditional_constat_auroc_rl: 0.61\n    traditional_dvd_auroc_sft: 0.68\n    traditional_dvd_auroc_rl: 0.55\n    dif_auroc_sft: 0.67\n    dif_auroc_rl: 0.54\n    dif_vs_traditional_auroc_gap_under_rl: 0.02\n    n_rl_models_available: 12\n    rl_model_cohort_size: 12\n  result_rationale: 'RL-robustness假设的理论基础是\"DIF操作在group-level ICC上，RL只平移不改变ICC形状\"。但worst\n    情景下RL不仅平移ICC——GRPO/PPO通过reward shaping改变了模型在不同difficulty levels上的response pattern，导致ICC形状本身变化（slope变陡或变平）。这使得RL-trained模型与SFT模型之间的ICC差异\n    既来自contamination也来自training method，DIF无法区分二者。DIF在RL cohort下power从0.42降到 0.29（retention\n    ratio=0.69），传统方法从~0.71降到~0.58。关键是DIF的降幅比例与传统方法相当， AUROC差距仅0.02——不足以支撑\"DIF是RL-orthogonal\n    signal\"的核心论点。此外，可获取的RL模型 仅12个（METABENCH中标注为RL-trained的开源模型有限），cohort太小导致DIF统计功效本身就低，\n    难以将power loss归因于RL vs simply small N。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 3: RL-Robustness Comparison — DIF vs Traditional Detectors'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - auroc_sft_cohort\n    - auroc_rl_cohort\n    - retention_ratio\n    - delta_auroc\n    rows:\n    - - DIF_ETS_C\n      - 0.67\n      - 0.54\n      - 0.81\n      - -0.13\n    - - Min-K%\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.78\n      - -0.16\n    - - ConStat\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.86\n      - -0.1\n    - - DVD\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.81\n      - -0.13\n    - - Perplexity\n      - 0.69\n      - 0.56\n      - 0.81\n      - -0.13\n  - title: 'Table 4: DIF TPR Under SFT vs RL Cohorts'\n    columns:\n    - effect_size\n    - tpr_sft_only\n    - tpr_with_rl\n    - retention\n    rows:\n    - - δ≥1.6\n      - 0.48\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.73\n    - - δ≥1.4\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.29\n      - 0.69\n    - - δ≥1.0\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.65\n    - - δ≥0.6\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.67\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 4: ROC curves for all 5 methods under SFT-only vs RL-included cohorts — all\n    curves shift left/down under RL, with DIF and traditional methods degrading similarly\n    (overlapping confidence intervals)'\n  - 'Fig 5: ICC comparison for 5 known-contaminated items — RL models show altered\n    slope (not just intercept shift), violating the theoretical basis of DIF robustness'\n  analysis: 'DIF的RL-robustness优势不显著。AUROC under RL: DIF 0.54 vs best traditional 0.61\n    (ConStat)， DIF实际上略差于ConStat。Power retention ratio 0.69落在worst tier预测范围[0.5, 0.75]内。\n    核心问题：RL改变ICC形状（discrimination parameter a也变化），不仅仅是difficulty shift， 这意味着DIF的理论robustness\n    argument不成立。加上RL cohort sample size仅12，统计结论的 可靠性本身存疑。无法支撑paper的headline claim。\n\n    '\n- name: constat_perturbation_eval\n  plan_id: plan_003a\n  description: '独立评估ConStat-style perturbation testing在MMLU上的contamination检测能力。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_0.6: 0.32\n    constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_1.0: 0.45\n    constat_tpr_non_rl_delta_ge_1.4: 0.55\n    constat_tpr_rl_delta_ge_0.6: 0.11\n    constat_tpr_rl_delta_ge_1.0: 0.18\n    constat_fpr: 0.06\n    constat_fdr_controlled_power: 0.28\n    n_perturbation_items_generated: 220\n    perturbation_quality_human_equiv_rate: 0.82\n    paraphrase_semantic_similarity: 0.91\n  result_rationale: 'ConStat在non-RL模型上有中等检测力（TPR=0.32 for δ≥0.6），因为SFT模型对verbatim\n    memorized items的perturbation确实敏感——答对原题但答错改写题是contamination的合理信号。 但在worst tier下：(1)\n    真实contamination多为partial memorization，模型可能只记住了answer pattern而非exact wording，对perturbation同样答对，降低sensitivity；(2)\n    LLM paraphrase 生成的reformulations质量参差——82%被判为semantically equivalent，但18%引入了微妙的\n    difficulty变化，增加noise；(3) RL模型对perturbation的sensitivity本身就低（RL鼓励 generalization），RL场景下TPR骤降至0.11。FDR-controlled\n    power仅0.28，意味着在控制 false discovery rate后，能检出的contaminated items不到三分之一。作为standalone\n    result 有一定baseline价值，但不足以独立成章。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 5: ConStat Perturbation Detection by Effect Size and Model Type'\n    columns:\n    - effect_size\n    - tpr_sft\n    - tpr_rl\n    - tpr_mixed\n    - fpr\n    rows:\n    - - δ≥1.4\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.06\n    - - δ≥1.0\n      - 0.45\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.06\n    - - δ≥0.6\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.11\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.07\n    - - δ≥0.4\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.07\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 6: ConStat detection power as function of perturbation intensity — diminishing\n    returns beyond moderate paraphrasing, suggesting contamination is not purely surface-form\n    dependent'\n  analysis: 'ConStat在non-RL场景下对large effects有moderate power，但RL场景下急剧退化。作为ensemble\n    component对non-RL覆盖有限值，但无法作为RL-robust complement to DIF（两者在RL下都弱）。 FDR-controlled\n    power 0.28意味着实际可用的detection capacity很有限。\n\n    '\n- name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n  plan_id: plan_003b\n  description: '独立评估DVD generation variance方法在MMLU上检测variant contamination的能力。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dvd_tpr_variant_contamination: 0.22\n    dvd_tpr_verbatim_contamination: 0.48\n    dvd_tpr_partial_contamination: 0.12\n    dvd_fpr: 0.09\n    dvd_auroc_overall: 0.61\n    n_models_evaluated: 13\n    n_items_sampled: 500\n    responses_per_item: 50\n    bimodal_distribution_rate_contaminated: 0.18\n    bimodal_distribution_rate_clean: 0.07\n    gpu_hours_used: 65\n  result_rationale: 'DVD的理论基础是contaminated items上model generation variance呈bimodal分布（有时recall\n    memorized answer，有时不能）。在worst tier下：(1) variant contamination（题目被改写后 contaminated）信号最弱——模型对variant的memorization不稳定，generation\n    variance与clean items差异小，TPR仅0.22；(2) partial contamination（仅记住部分信息）几乎无法检测（TPR=0.12），\n    因为partial memory不产生bimodal response pattern，而是持续的uncertainty；(3) 即使verbatim contamination，TPR也仅0.48，因为很多模型在temperature\n    sampling下对已知答案也表现stable （always correct），generation variance反而很低——与clean but easy\n    items难以区分；(4) bimodal rate在contaminated items上仅18% vs clean items 7%，差异有统计显著性但effect\n    size 太小无法做reliable detection。FPR=0.09偏高。总计消耗65 GPU hours，性价比低。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 6: DVD Detection by Contamination Type'\n    columns:\n    - contamination_type\n    - tpr\n    - fpr\n    - auroc\n    - n_items\n    rows:\n    - - verbatim\n      - 0.48\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.72\n      - 120\n    - - variant\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.58\n      - 180\n    - - partial\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.52\n      - 200\n    - - overall\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.61\n      - 500\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 7: Generation variance distributions for contaminated vs clean items — overlapping\n    distributions with small separation, bimodal pattern only visible in subset of\n    verbatim contamination cases'\n  analysis: 'DVD对variant contamination的检测力远低于预期（TPR=0.22 vs 论文claim需要的高coverage）。\n    核心问题是real-world contamination不产生clean bimodal response pattern——partial memorization\n    导致diffuse variance而非bimodal variance。GPU开销大但回报低，作为ensemble component 贡献有限。\n\n    '\n- name: ensemble_fusion\n  plan_id: plan_003c\n  description: '将DIF + ConStat + DVD融合为多信号ensemble，评估覆盖度和precision。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    ensemble_tpr_full_spectrum: 0.42\n    ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_1.4: 0.52\n    ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_1.0: 0.3\n    ensemble_tpr_delta_ge_0.6: 0.18\n    ensemble_fpr: 0.11\n    ensemble_f1: 0.35\n    majority_voting_tpr: 0.38\n    weighted_fusion_tpr: 0.42\n    signal_correlation_dif_constat: 0.61\n    signal_correlation_dif_dvd: 0.54\n    signal_correlation_constat_dvd: 0.58\n    unique_items_flagged_by_only_one_signal_pct: 0.15\n    items_flagged_by_all_three_pct: 0.42\n  result_rationale: 'Ensemble假设三个signal互补——DIF覆盖large effects+RL场景，ConStat覆盖non-RL\n    medium effects， DVD覆盖variant contamination。但worst tier下：(1) 三个signal之间correlation高（r=0.54-0.61），\n    表明它们largely flag同一批items而非互补覆盖不同盲区；(2) 仅15%的items被unique地由某一个 signal单独检出，说明\"互补覆盖\"理论不成立——各signal的failure\n    modes相关（都在partial/medium effect上失败）；(3) 42%的items被三个signal同时flag，说明easy cases三者都能检出但hard\n    cases 三者都漏检；(4) FPR=0.11，majority voting无法有效压低FPR因为false positives也呈相关模式 （architecture-driven\n    spurious DIF也往往在perturbation testing中产生false positive）。 Weighted fusion比majority\n    voting略好（TPR 0.42 vs 0.38）但提升有限。整体full-spectrum TPR=0.42落在worst tier [0.35, 0.6]范围内，不足以作为实用detection\n    system。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 7: Ensemble vs Individual Signal Performance'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - tpr_ge_1.4\n    - tpr_ge_1.0\n    - tpr_ge_0.6\n    - fpr\n    - f1\n    rows:\n    - - DIF_only\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.25\n    - - ConStat_only\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.32\n    - - DVD_only\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.18\n    - - Majority_2of3\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.11\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.3\n    - - Weighted_fusion\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.11\n      - 0.35\n  - title: 'Table 8: Signal Correlation Matrix'\n    columns:\n    - signal_pair\n    - pearson_r\n    - overlap_in_flagged_items_pct\n    rows:\n    - - DIF-ConStat\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.68\n    - - DIF-DVD\n      - 0.54\n      - 0.59\n    - - ConStat-DVD\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.63\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 8: Venn diagram of items flagged by each signal — large central overlap,\n    small unique regions, contradicting the ''complementary coverage'' hypothesis'\n  - 'Fig 9: Ensemble TPR as function of effect size — flat improvement over best individual\n    signal, no ''coverage completion'' effect at medium/low effects'\n  analysis: 'Ensemble的\"互补覆盖\"核心假设不成立。信号间高相关（0.54-0.61）意味着ensemble主要在置信度上 提升（对已检出items更confident）而非在覆盖度上提升（检出新items）。Weighted\n    fusion的TPR=0.42 仅比best individual signal (ConStat 0.30 at δ≥1.0) 提升有限，且FPR=0.11偏高。这个ensemble\n    不能作为\"full-spectrum detection system\"呈现——更准确的描述是\"three weak signals with correlated\n    failure modes\"。\n\n    '\n- name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '在GSM8K上复制DIF分析，以GSM1K作为contamination ground truth进行交叉验证。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gsm8k_gsm1k_gap_dif_correlation_spearman: 0.11\n    gsm8k_gsm1k_gap_dif_correlation_pearson: 0.08\n    dif_tpr_gsm8k_delta_ge_1.4: 0.3\n    dif_fpr_gsm8k: 0.13\n    n_models_with_both_gsm8k_gsm1k: 48\n    irt_model_fit_rmsea_gsm8k: 0.09\n    gsm8k_item_discrimination_mean: 0.85\n    gsm1k_gap_mean_across_models: 0.07\n    gsm1k_gap_std: 0.11\n    n_items_gsm8k_analyzed: 1319\n  result_rationale: 'GSM8K validation在worst tier下面临多重困难：(1) 可获取的同时有GSM8K和GSM1K结果的模型仅\n    约48个（远少于MMLU的5055个），DIF统计功效严重不足；(2) GSM8K是math benchmark，item discrimination偏低(mean\n    a=0.85)因为数学题的对错更binary、less informative about latent ability gradient，这直接降低DIF\n    detection power；(3) GSM8K-GSM1K gap本身noisy（std=0.11 vs mean=0.07），gap的model-level\n    variance高说明contamination不是uniform的——不同模型 contamination程度差异大，但DIF是item-level metric，model-level\n    gap与item-level DIF flag之间的mapping本就不是直接对应的；(4) GSM1K作为ground truth的assumption是\"GSM1K\n    uncontaminated\"，但GSM1K发布后也可能被contaminated，ground truth本身会退化。 Spearman rho=0.11几乎无相关，无法支撑cross-benchmark\n    generalizability。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 9: GSM8K Cross-Validation Results'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - worst_tier_range\n    - verdict\n    rows:\n    - - DIF_TPR_δ≥1.4\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.25-0.50\n      - IN_RANGE\n    - - DIF_FPR\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.08-0.15\n      - IN_RANGE\n    - - GSM8K-GSM1K_gap_correlation\n      - 0.11\n      - 0.0-0.18\n      - IN_RANGE\n    - - N_models\n      - 48\n      - ≥50 desired\n      - INSUFFICIENT\n    - - IRT_fit_RMSEA\n      - 0.09\n      - ≤0.06\n      - FAIL\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 10: Scatter plot of per-model GSM8K-GSM1K gap vs number of DIF-flagged items\n    in that model''s performance — near-zero correlation with wide scatter'\n  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark validation为negative result。GSM8K上DIF表现与MMLU类似（low TPR,\n    high FPR）， 且与GSM1K ground truth的correlation接近零（rho=0.11）。样本量不足（48 models vs desired\n    50+） 进一步削弱统计结论的可靠性。这不能作为DIF generalizability的支撑证据。\n\n    '\n- name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '在METABENCH MMLU数据上拟合bifactor IRT模型，选取anchor items，执行equating pilot。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    bifactor_convergence: partial\n    bifactor_iterations_to_convergence: 8500\n    bifactor_n_items_converged: 9200\n    bifactor_n_items_failed: 3308\n    general_factor_variance_explained: 0.35\n    n_specific_factors: 57\n    specific_factor_avg_loading: 0.28\n    anchor_item_n_selected: 380\n    anchor_item_stability_mean_dif: 0.15\n    equating_spearman_rho_before: 0.82\n    equating_spearman_rho_after: 0.85\n    equating_rank_displacement_mean: 3.2\n    equating_rank_displacement_p95: 12\n    score_reliability_original: 0.94\n    score_reliability_equated: 0.89\n  result_rationale: 'Bifactor model在5055个异构模型上面临严重的estimation challenge：(1) 57个MMLU\n    subjects作为 specific factors，加上1个general factor，parameter space巨大（~12500 items\n    × 3 parameters × 58 factors），在worst tier下3308个items（26%）的参数估计不收敛或产生Heywood cases\n    （negative variance estimates）；(2) general factor仅解释35%的variance——这意味着MMLU 不是primarily\n    measuring一个general LLM ability，而是highly multidimensional的，bifactor structure不是good\n    fit；(3) specific factor loadings平均仅0.28，说明subject-level factors 也很弱，很多items不清晰地load在任何factor上——factor\n    structure不可解释；(4) 尽管如此， equating在技术上仍可执行：选出380个stable anchor items（无DIF、参数估计收敛），equating\n    后ranking correlation从0.82提升到0.85，但这个提升幅度小（Δ=0.03），且基线rho=0.82 已低于Claim 3要求的0.95标准。Equating没有失败但也没有convincingly成功——它能small\n    improvement ranking stability，但不能达到psychometric equivalence的标准。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 10: Bifactor IRT Model Fit and Equating Results'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - target\n    - verdict\n    rows:\n    - - convergence_rate\n      - 73.5%\n      - ≥95%\n      - FAIL\n    - - general_factor_variance\n      - 0.35\n      - ≥0.50\n      - WEAK\n    - - anchor_items_available\n      - 380\n      - ≥500\n      - MARGINAL\n    - - equating_rho\n      - 0.85\n      - ≥0.95\n      - FAIL\n    - - rank_displacement_p95\n      - 12\n      - ≤5\n      - FAIL\n    - - score_reliability_post\n      - 0.89\n      - ≥0.92\n      - MARGINAL\n  - title: 'Table 11: Factor Structure Summary'\n    columns:\n    - factor_type\n    - n_factors\n    - mean_loading\n    - pct_items_loading_gt_0.3\n    rows:\n    - - general\n      - 1\n      - 0.42\n      - 62%\n    - - specific_STEM\n      - 14\n      - 0.31\n      - 38%\n    - - specific_humanities\n      - 18\n      - 0.26\n      - 29%\n    - - specific_social_science\n      - 15\n      - 0.28\n      - 33%\n    - - specific_other\n      - 10\n      - 0.24\n      - 25%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 11: Scree plot showing eigenvalues — no clear elbow, gradual decline suggesting\n    no dominant general factor'\n  - 'Fig 12: Equated vs original model rankings — scatter with regression line showing\n    moderate but not strong agreement (rho=0.85), notable outliers at tails'\n  analysis: 'Bifactor model在异构LLM population上partially converges但factor structure不清晰。\n    General factor太弱（35% variance）挑战了\"MMLU measures a coherent construct\"的前提。 Equating产生了modest\n    improvement (0.82→0.85) 但远未达到psychometric equivalence标准 (0.95)。作为独立贡献（Claim 3\n    standalone），这个result需要被framed为\"benchmark multidimensionality的empirical characterization\"而非\"successful\n    equating\"。可能可以 pivot到Growing Pains style的\"LLM evaluation需要multidimensional IRT\"叙事。\n\n    '\n- name: item_generation_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '生成替代items并通过student simulation进行calibration，评估difficulty estimation质量。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_items_generated: 150\n    n_items_passing_quality_filter: 112\n    difficulty_calibration_rho_student_sim: 0.48\n    difficulty_calibration_rho_prompt_based: 0.22\n    difficulty_mae_student_sim: 0.85\n    difficulty_mae_prompt_based: 1.45\n    discrimination_calibration_rho: 0.31\n    construct_alignment_rate: 0.72\n    holdout_validation_rho: 0.44\n    student_sim_correlation_with_real_models: 0.52\n    gpu_hours_used: 180\n  result_rationale: 'Item generation在worst tier下的核心问题：(1) Student simulation (arXiv\n    2601.09953) 的difficulty estimation在MMLU上表现弱于其在其他benchmarks上的reported results——因为\n    MMLU covers 57 diverse subjects，student simulation的\"simulated students\"是single\n    LLM 做capability ablation，但不同subject需要不同type的knowledge/reasoning，single-model simulation无法capture\n    this diversity，rho=0.48；(2) Prompt-based difficulty targeting 依然很差（rho=0.22），与文献报告一致；(3)\n    Student simulation比prompt-based好（0.48 vs 0.22） 但absolute accuracy仍不够——difficulty\n    MAE=0.85 logits意味着平均偏差接近1个标准差， 生成的items实际difficulty与target可能差1-2个difficulty band；(4)\n    Discrimination calibration 更差（rho=0.31），因为discrimination是更subtle的item property，依赖于item如何在不同ability\n    levels上区分模型，student simulation几乎无法capture；(5) Construct alignment rate 72% 意味着28%的generated\n    items虽然表面上是同一subject但实际测量的cognitive process不同 （e.g., 要求recall的item被替换为要求reasoning的item）。这些result不支撑\"calibrated\n    item regeneration\"的claim，但student sim vs prompt-based的comparison本身有文献价值。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 12: Item Calibration Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - difficulty_rho\n    - difficulty_mae\n    - discrimination_rho\n    - construct_alignment\n    rows:\n    - - student_simulation\n      - 0.48\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.31\n      - 72%\n    - - prompt_based\n      - 0.22\n      - 1.45\n      - 0.18\n      - 65%\n    - - random_baseline\n      - 0.05\n      - 1.8\n      - 0.08\n      - 45%\n  - title: 'Table 13: Holdout Validation on 30 Models'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - student_sim\n    - prompt_based\n    rows:\n    - - difficulty_rank_correlation\n      - 0.44\n      - 0.19\n    - - score_equivalence_rho\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.68\n    - - ranking_preservation_top10\n      - 70%\n      - 50%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 13: Predicted vs actual item difficulty — student simulation shows moderate\n    correlation but with substantial scatter, especially for very hard items'\n  - 'Fig 14: Distribution of difficulty estimation errors — student simulation has\n    tighter but still wide distribution (SD=0.85) compared to prompt-based (SD=1.2)'\n  analysis: 'Student simulation在MMLU上的calibration quality不足以支撑reliable item replacement。\n    Difficulty rho=0.48意味着替换后的benchmark与原版在difficulty ordering上只有moderate agreement，不够做psychometric\n    equating。但student sim vs prompt-based的comparison （0.48 vs 0.22）以及failure mode\n    analysis（which subjects/difficulty ranges失败） 仍有独立的文献贡献价值。\n\n    '\n- name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: '实现cumulative Bayesian DIF priors，模拟4次successive benchmark administrations的power积累。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    single_admin_power_delta_1.0: 0.15\n    cumulative_power_2_admins_delta_1.0: 0.22\n    cumulative_power_3_admins_delta_1.0: 0.3\n    cumulative_power_4_admins_delta_1.0: 0.38\n    single_admin_power_delta_1.4: 0.35\n    cumulative_power_4_admins_delta_1.4: 0.55\n    bayesian_fpr_single: 0.1\n    bayesian_fpr_cumulative_4: 0.08\n    prior_informativeness_shrinkage: 0.45\n  result_rationale: 'Bayesian cumulative priors在worst tier下受到两个因素制约：(1) 如果baseline\n    single-admin power已经很低（0.15 for δ=1.0，因为real data上IRT model misfit），那么cumulative\n    evidence accumulation的起点就低——Bayesian updating from a weak prior仍然是weak， 4次admin后仅到0.38（远低于theoretical\n    prediction of 0.70）；(2) Prior informativeness 受model population heterogeneity影响——如果每次administration的model\n    cohort composition 很不同（architecture mix变化），prior从上一admin的posterior transfer不顺畅，shrinkage\n    factor高达0.45（理想应<0.2），意味着prior对posterior的influence被data overwhelm但data 本身noisy。FPR从0.10降至0.08是modest\n    improvement。总体而言，cumulative approach能 提升power但幅度远不如simulated homogeneous scenarios中的预期。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 14: Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power Accumulation'\n    columns:\n    - n_administrations\n    - power_delta_1.0\n    - power_delta_1.4\n    - fpr\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.1\n    - - 2\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.09\n    - - 3\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.49\n      - 0.09\n    - - 4\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.08\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 15: Power accumulation curves — shallow slope compared to theoretical prediction\n    (dashed line), gap widens with each administration due to population heterogeneity'\n  analysis: 'Cumulative Bayesian approach有边际收益但无法rescue低baseline power。4 admins后power\n    仅从0.15升至0.38 (δ=1.0)，远低于theoretical 0.70。Population heterogeneity导致prior transfer效率低。作为P2\n    experiment，结果不改变overall narrative但进一步确认了DIF在 heterogeneous LLM population上的fundamental\n    limitations。\n\n    '\n- name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: '分析benchmark在progressive item replacement下的validity degradation。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    ranking_stability_5pct_replaced: 0.94\n    ranking_stability_10pct_replaced: 0.88\n    ranking_stability_20pct_replaced: 0.79\n    ranking_stability_50pct_replaced: 0.62\n    score_reliability_5pct: 0.92\n    score_reliability_10pct: 0.88\n    score_reliability_20pct: 0.81\n    score_reliability_50pct: 0.67\n    construct_coverage_5pct: 0.97\n    construct_coverage_10pct: 0.93\n    construct_coverage_20pct: 0.85\n    construct_coverage_50pct: 0.71\n    critical_replacement_threshold: 0.12\n  result_rationale: 'Graceful degradation在worst tier下退化快于预期因为：(1) Item calibration\n    quality差 （difficulty rho=0.48 from plan_006），替换items的psychometric properties与被替换items\n    不匹配，每次替换引入的error大于calibration error budget允许的范围；(2) Bifactor equating 不充分（rho=0.85\n    from plan_005），equating本身引入systematic bias，累积到20%替换时 ranking stability降至0.79（如果equating完美，应维持在0.92+）；(3)\n    Construct coverage degradation因为28%的generated items construct alignment有问题（from\n    plan_006）， 20%替换时约5-6%的items测量不同construct，coverage降至0.85。Critical threshold（ranking\n    rho降至0.90以下的替换比例）仅12%——意味着实际上只能安全替换约1500个items，远少于 potential contaminated items的数量（如果FPR=0.12则约1800个被flag）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 15: Validity Degradation Under Progressive Replacement'\n    columns:\n    - replacement_pct\n    - ranking_rho\n    - reliability\n    - construct_coverage\n    rows:\n    - - 0% (baseline)\n      - 1.0\n      - 0.94\n      - 1.0\n    - - 5%\n      - 0.94\n      - 0.92\n      - 0.97\n    - - 10%\n      - 0.88\n      - 0.88\n      - 0.93\n    - - 20%\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.81\n      - 0.85\n    - - 50%\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.67\n      - 0.71\n  - title: 'Table 16: Critical Thresholds'\n    columns:\n    - validity_criterion\n    - threshold_value\n    - max_safe_replacement_pct\n    rows:\n    - - ranking_rho_≥0.90\n      - 0.9\n      - 12%\n    - - reliability_≥0.90\n      - 0.9\n      - 7%\n    - - construct_coverage_≥0.90\n      - 0.9\n      - 14%\n    - - all_criteria_met\n      - '-'\n      - 7%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 16: Validity metrics as function of replacement rate — all three metrics\n    degrade faster than linear, with reliability being the binding constraint (7%)'\n  analysis: 'Graceful degradation analysis表明在当前calibration quality下，只能安全替换7%的items\n    （约875个items，满足所有validity criteria）。这远不足以构成practical \"self-healing\" benchmark——如果检测到的contaminated\n    items超过7%，replacement会损害benchmark validity。 这是对Claim 3的严重限制，但degradation curve本身是有价值的empirical\n    contribution， 可以frame为\"item replacement的practical bounds\"。\n\n    '\n- name: item_focused_trees\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: '实现Item-Focused Trees，将model release date作为continuous covariate替代categorical\n    cohort DIF。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    ift_tpr_delta_ge_1.4: 0.33\n    ift_tpr_delta_ge_1.0: 0.16\n    ift_fpr: 0.1\n    ift_vs_categorical_dif_tpr_delta: -0.05\n    ift_computation_time_hours: 18\n    n_splits_found: 3.2\n    split_dates_concentration: 2023-06 to 2024-01\n    overfitting_cross_val_tpr_drop: 0.12\n  result_rationale: 'Item-Focused Trees理论上避免arbitrary cohort splits，但在worst tier下：(1)\n    Release date 作为continuous covariate与contamination的关系不是smooth monotonic的——contamination是\n    event-driven（某次data leak），不是gradual trend，IFT的tree structure可以capture这个 但容易overfit到特定split\n    points；(2) Cross-validation显示TPR drop=0.12，说明overfitting significant；(3) 在model\n    heterogeneity高的情况下，IFT实际上比categorical DIF表现略差 （TPR差-0.05），因为tree splitting在high-noise环境下容易找到spurious\n    splits——3.2个 average splits集中在2023年中到2024年初，这恰好是architecture transition period\n    （GPT-4发布后大量models涌现），tree可能在capture architecture shift而非contamination。 FPR=0.10比categorical\n    DIF（0.12）略低，但improvement不显著。Computation cost 18 hours 因为per-item tree fitting在12508\n    items上。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 17: Item-Focused Trees vs Categorical DIF'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - categorical_dif\n    - ift\n    - delta\n    rows:\n    - - TPR_δ≥1.4\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.33\n      - -0.05\n    - - TPR_δ≥1.0\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.16\n      - -0.02\n    - - FPR\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.1\n      - -0.02\n    - - F1\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.24\n      - -0.01\n    - - computation_hours\n      - 0.5\n      - 18\n      - '+17.5'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 17: IFT split point distribution — concentration around architecture transition\n    periods rather than known contamination events'\n  analysis: IFT未能改善DIF detection。Split points与architecture transitions而非contamination\n    events 对齐，进一步证实model heterogeneity是dominant signal source。计算成本高36倍但无performance\n    gain。作为P2 experiment，结论是negative：continuous covariate treatment不解决fundamental\n    问题。\n","numLines":877,"startLine":1,"totalLines":877}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UtmoS8hxWxM86ARaJ6SePF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've read the PDF and the review context YAML. Now I need to conduct a full review with 2 reviewers following the dispatch template:\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nThen a full roundtable: Step 1 (independent reviews) → Step 2 (cross-sharing) → Step 3 (convergence) → Step 4 (synthesis).\n\nLet me dispatch both reviewers in parallel as agents, then conduct the roundtable.\n\nLet me launch R1 and R2 as parallel agents.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35020,"cache_read_input_tokens":23077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35020},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"570af1f9-c3cd-4db4-aa61-2d20e9ee2d29","uuid":"babdab4a-7dc9-4ceb-87a6-990d0fcf652a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UtmoS8hxWxM86ARaJ6SePF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PDF 和实验设计上下文已读取。启动两位 Reviewer 并行独立审稿。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35020,"cache_read_input_tokens":23077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35020},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"570af1f9-c3cd-4db4-aa61-2d20e9ee2d29","uuid":"59e0393f-e2db-4578-86d7-a92ccc783f6d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UtmoS8hxWxM86ARaJ6SePF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01THHYhuTrJxSkgWh7JPy8yR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus is **methodology and experimental rigor**.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"When Psychometric Contamination Detection Meets Heterogeneous Model Populations: A Negative-Result Study on DIF-Based Benchmark Monitoring\"\n\nThe paper investigates whether Differential Item Functioning (DIF)—a classical psychometric technique—can serve as an RL-robust contamination signal for LLM benchmark evaluation. The core finding is **negative**: the unidimensional IRT model required for DIF severely misfits the heterogeneous 5,000+ model population (RMSEA=0.11, CFI=0.78), architecture differences generate massive spurious DIF (FPR=0.12), and the claimed RL-robustness advantage is not observed (DIF AUROC=0.54 under RL vs ConStat 0.61). Additional experiments on ensemble fusion, bifactor IRT equating, item generation, cumulative Bayesian DIF, graceful degradation, and cross-benchmark validation (GSM8K) all yield weak or negative results.\n\n## Paper Content (8 pages + tables)\n\n### Abstract\nBenchmark contamination threatens the validity of LLM evaluation, yet existing detection methods degrade under RL training. They test DIF on METABENCH (5,055 models × 12,508 MMLU items) and cross-validate on GSM8K with GSM1K ground truth. Findings are predominantly negative. IRT model severely misfits (RMSEA=0.11, CFI=0.78), architecture differences inflate FPR to 0.12. DIF AUROC=0.54 under RL, worse than ConStat (0.61). Three-signal ensemble fails complementary coverage (r=0.54-0.61). Bifactor equating partial convergence (73.5%), ρ=0.85 vs required ≥0.95. Max safe item replacement: 7%.\n\n### Method (Section 3)\n- 3.1: DIF-Based Detection: Temporal cohort partitioning (pre/post-2024), 2PL IRT model, Mantel-Haenszel DIF statistic with ETS C criterion\n- 3.2: Multi-Signal Ensemble: DIF + ConStat + DVD, majority voting and weighted fusion\n- 3.3: Bifactor IRT Equating: bifactor model with general + 57 subject-specific factors, anchor items for equating, student simulation for item generation\n\n### Experiments (Section 4) — 10 experiments + 1 supplementary\n1. DIF on MMLU: TPR=0.38 (δ≥1.4), FPR=0.12, MMLU-CF ϕ=0.09. All IRT fit indices FAIL.\n2. RL-Robustness: DIF AUROC=0.54 (RL) vs ConStat 0.61. Only 12 RL models. Power retention 0.69.\n3. ConStat: TPR=0.55 (SFT, δ≥1.4), drops to 0.18 under RL. FDR-controlled power=0.28.\n4. DVD: Overall TPR=0.25, AUROC=0.61. Partial contamination TPR=0.12.\n5. Ensemble: Weighted fusion F1=0.35, signal correlations 0.54-0.61, 42% three-way overlap.\n6. GSM8K cross-validation: DIF TPR=0.30, FPR=0.13, GSM1K correlation=0.11. Only 48 models.\n7. Bifactor IRT: 73.5% convergence, general factor 35% variance, equating ρ=0.85, rank displacement p95=12.\n8. Item calibration: Student sim ρ=0.48, prompt-based ρ=0.22. Difficulty MAE=0.85. 28% construct misalignment.\n9. Cumulative Bayesian DIF: 4 admins → power 0.38 (δ=1.0) vs theoretical 0.70.\n10. Graceful degradation: Max safe replacement 7%. Reliability binding at 7%.\n11. (Supplementary) Item-Focused Trees: No improvement over categorical DIF, 36× cost.\n\n### Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\nThe paper's imagined experiments include all 10 experiments above plus IFT. The review_context indicates this is a \"worst tier\" scenario where the core DIF hypothesis fails. Key expected metrics match closely with what's reported.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate **methodology and experimental rigor** specifically:\n\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Are the methods correctly applied? Are there flaws in experimental design?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Sample sizes, significance testing, effect sizes, multiple comparisons\n3. **Experimental coverage**: Are there missing experiments or controls? Does the experiment design support the claims?\n4. **Reproducibility**: Is enough detail provided?\n5. **Internal consistency**: Do the results tell a coherent story?\n\n### Specific questions to address:\n- Is the 2PL unidimensional IRT model the right starting point, or should they have gone directly to multidimensional IRT?\n- Is 12 RL models enough to draw conclusions about RL robustness?\n- How should we assess ground truth quality (MMLU-CF, GSM1K)?\n- Are the IRT fit diagnostics correctly applied and interpreted?\n- Is the graceful degradation analysis methodologically sound?\n- Are the negative results convincingly established (vs merely inconclusive)?\n\nProduce a structured review with:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, with severity: minor/moderate/major)\n- Questions for Authors (numbered)\n- Missing Experiments or Controls\n- Preliminary Score (1-6) with confidence (low/medium/high)\n- Score justification (2-3 sentences)\n","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35020,"cache_read_input_tokens":23077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35020},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"570af1f9-c3cd-4db4-aa61-2d20e9ee2d29","uuid":"51606421-fffb-4fd1-973b-4e2b7207a899"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"ae9f1fb126a2cf1ff","tool_use_id":"toolu_01THHYhuTrJxSkgWh7JPy8yR","description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus is **methodology and experimental rigor**.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"When Psychometric Contamination Detection Meets Heterogeneous Model Populations: A Negative-Result Study on DIF-Based Benchmark Monitoring\"\n\nThe paper investigates whether Differential Item Functioning (DIF)—a classical psychometric technique—can serve as an RL-robust contamination signal for LLM benchmark evaluation. The core finding is **negative**: the unidimensional IRT model required for DIF severely misfits the heterogeneous 5,000+ model population (RMSEA=0.11, CFI=0.78), architecture differences generate massive spurious DIF (FPR=0.12), and the claimed RL-robustness advantage is not observed (DIF AUROC=0.54 under RL vs ConStat 0.61). Additional experiments on ensemble fusion, bifactor IRT equating, item generation, cumulative Bayesian DIF, graceful degradation, and cross-benchmark validation (GSM8K) all yield weak or negative results.\n\n## Paper Content (8 pages + tables)\n\n### Abstract\nBenchmark contamination threatens the validity of LLM evaluation, yet existing detection methods degrade under RL training. They test DIF on METABENCH (5,055 models × 12,508 MMLU items) and cross-validate on GSM8K with GSM1K ground truth. Findings are predominantly negative. IRT model severely misfits (RMSEA=0.11, CFI=0.78), architecture differences inflate FPR to 0.12. DIF AUROC=0.54 under RL, worse than ConStat (0.61). Three-signal ensemble fails complementary coverage (r=0.54-0.61). Bifactor equating partial convergence (73.5%), ρ=0.85 vs required ≥0.95. Max safe item replacement: 7%.\n\n### Method (Section 3)\n- 3.1: DIF-Based Detection: Temporal cohort partitioning (pre/post-2024), 2PL IRT model, Mantel-Haenszel DIF statistic with ETS C criterion\n- 3.2: Multi-Signal Ensemble: DIF + ConStat + DVD, majority voting and weighted fusion\n- 3.3: Bifactor IRT Equating: bifactor model with general + 57 subject-specific factors, anchor items for equating, student simulation for item generation\n\n### Experiments (Section 4) — 10 experiments + 1 supplementary\n1. DIF on MMLU: TPR=0.38 (δ≥1.4), FPR=0.12, MMLU-CF ϕ=0.09. All IRT fit indices FAIL.\n2. RL-Robustness: DIF AUROC=0.54 (RL) vs ConStat 0.61. Only 12 RL models. Power retention 0.69.\n3. ConStat: TPR=0.55 (SFT, δ≥1.4), drops to 0.18 under RL. FDR-controlled power=0.28.\n4. DVD: Overall TPR=0.25, AUROC=0.61. Partial contamination TPR=0.12.\n5. Ensemble: Weighted fusion F1=0.35, signal correlations 0.54-0.61, 42% three-way overlap.\n6. GSM8K cross-validation: DIF TPR=0.30, FPR=0.13, GSM1K correlation=0.11. Only 48 models.\n7. Bifactor IRT: 73.5% convergence, general factor 35% variance, equating ρ=0.85, rank displacement p95=12.\n8. Item calibration: Student sim ρ=0.48, prompt-based ρ=0.22. Difficulty MAE=0.85. 28% construct misalignment.\n9. Cumulative Bayesian DIF: 4 admins → power 0.38 (δ=1.0) vs theoretical 0.70.\n10. Graceful degradation: Max safe replacement 7%. Reliability binding at 7%.\n11. (Supplementary) Item-Focused Trees: No improvement over categorical DIF, 36× cost.\n\n### Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\nThe paper's imagined experiments include all 10 experiments above plus IFT. The review_context indicates this is a \"worst tier\" scenario where the core DIF hypothesis fails. Key expected metrics match closely with what's reported.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate **methodology and experimental rigor** specifically:\n\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Are the methods correctly applied? Are there flaws in experimental design?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Sample sizes, significance testing, effect sizes, multiple comparisons\n3. **Experimental coverage**: Are there missing experiments or controls? Does the experiment design support the claims?\n4. **Reproducibility**: Is enough detail provided?\n5. **Internal consistency**: Do the results tell a coherent story?\n\n### Specific questions to address:\n- Is the 2PL unidimensional IRT model the right starting point, or should they have gone directly to multidimensional IRT?\n- Is 12 RL models enough to draw conclusions about RL robustness?\n- How should we assess ground truth quality (MMLU-CF, GSM1K)?\n- Are the IRT fit diagnostics correctly applied and interpreted?\n- Is the graceful degradation analysis methodologically sound?\n- Are the negative results convincingly established (vs merely inconclusive)?\n\nProduce a structured review with:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, with severity: minor/moderate/major)\n- Questions for Authors (numbered)\n- Missing Experiments or Controls\n- Preliminary Score (1-6) with confidence (low/medium/high)\n- Score justification (2-3 sentences)\n","uuid":"4dd47783-3f55-4010-a793-d6de4ff33f45","session_id":"570af1f9-c3cd-4db4-aa61-2d20e9ee2d29"}
